---
// Deliberately editorial prose, not a three-card "how it works" grid —
// the client-experience story reads better as flowing text than as
// process steps, and it keeps this page from feeling like another
// service page.
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import portrait from "../../assets/about/sarah-portrait.jpg";
---

<section class="section section--dark surface-leather working-with-lenz">
  <div class="container working-with-lenz__inner">
    <div class="working-with-lenz__text">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Working With LENZ</p>
        <h2>You're Working With Sarah — Not a Sales Team</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="working-with-lenz__copy">
        <p>
          When you reach out to LENZ, you're talking directly to the person who will be behind the
          camera or flying the drone. There's no handoff between a sales call and the actual shoot
          — the same person planning your project is the one creating the imagery, from the first
          conversation to final delivery.
        </p>
        <p>
          That matters for consistency. Photography and aerial work are treated as one capability,
          not two separate services — a listing, a commercial property, or a construction site can
          get ground photography and professional aerial coverage from the same shoot, planned
          together rather than booked separately.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every image is created with where it's actually going to be used in mind — a listing, a
          website, an ad campaign, social media, print, or other marketing — not just captured and
          handed over. And while LENZ is based in western Iowa, travel is available for commercial
          and specialty projects across the wider region.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="working-with-lenz__portrait">
      <Image src={portrait} alt="Portrait of Sarah Lenz, LENZ founder and photographer" width={800} widths={[400, 600, 800]} sizes="(min-width: 55em) 28vw, 70vw" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .working-with-lenz__copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1em;
    max-width: 42rem;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--color-muted-on-dark);
  }

  .working-with-lenz__portrait {
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
    max-width: 20rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(224, 176, 104, 0.16);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .working-with-lenz__portrait :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media (min-width: 55em) {
    .working-with-lenz__inner {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }

    .working-with-lenz__text {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .working-with-lenz__portrait {
      flex-shrink: 0;
      width: 20rem;
      max-width: 26vw;
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
